      ":question/problem": "Consider the following differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}+4y=2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation can be written as\n\n$$\ny(x)=A\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x+B\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x+g(x),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are constants. Which of the following could be the function $g(x)?$\n\n*Hint: Use the variation of parameters method. You may also wish to make use of the following results (integration constants omitted):*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}\u20612x\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x & =x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x|-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
